# The relayer's Dockerfile takes the REPO ROOT as its build context — it needs shared/ and two
# deployment JSONs from app/ — so without this file `fly deploy` uploads all ~2 GB of the tree,
# node_modules and .git included. Measured 2026-08-20: the upload was crawling at roughly 50 KB/s
# and would not have finished inside a working day, which is what a deploy that "hangs" actually
# was. The image needs about 200 KB of source.
#
# Keep this list ALLOW-anything/DENY-the-heavy-things rather than a whitelist: the Dockerfile
# copies specific paths, so anything unlisted here is simply never used, and a whitelist would
# silently break the next file the relayer starts reading.

**/node_modules
.git
**/dist
**/.vercel
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.venv
**/venv

# Build artefacts and releases — tens of MB of zips that no image layer touches.
*.zip
*.zip.sha256
**/*.wasm
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Big binaries and captures that live in the repo for the site and the docs.
assets
docs/screenshots
site
**/*.mp4
**/*.mov

# Nothing in the image ever reads these.
extension
extension-x
contracts
codec
test
bench
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Local tooling and scratch state that is not source at all — each of these alone was bigger than
# the image: a 38 MB cloudflared binary, Chrome dev profiles, model caches, agent worktrees.
.tools
.claude
**/.dev-profiles
**/.cache
**/*.pkl
